      "value": "The Great Speckled Bird was published from 1968 to 1976 with some issues appearing in the 1980s and 2000s.  This publication was one of the longest-running and highest quality underground newspapers of the era.  Frequently published were articles on Atlanta's political leaders, the women's movement, abortion, racial issues, popular culture and gay liberation."
